<aside class="page-toc"><p class="page-toc-title">On this page</p><nav aria-label="On this page"><a href="#available">Publications from the programme</a><a href="#specification">Galapagensis Technical Specification</a><a href="#foundation">Related foundational work</a><a href="#offline">Galapagensis to go</a><a href="#reuse">Citation and reuse</a></nav></aside>
<article class="page-prose"><section id="available" class="prose-section"><h2>Publications from the programme</h2><p>Galapagensis publishes research on the history, documentary memory and knowledge of the Galápagos Islands, together with the methodological work that supports those investigations. Publications will include research monographs, recovered historical texts, critical editions, documentary compilations, photographic and thematic books, scholarly articles and educational resources.</p><p>The works available below introduce the programme’s methodological framework and its intellectual foundations. Further publications will connect readers with historical sources, the contexts in which they were produced, and the research developed around them.</p></section><section id="specification" class="prose-section"><h2>Galapagensis Technical Specification</h2><p><em>Method and Data Model for Relational Documentary Research in Galápagos History, Knowledge and Memory</em></p><p>Edgardo Civallero · 2026 · Version 1.4 · English</p><p>The methodological and data-model framework for connecting dispersed sources, documenting evidence-backed relationships, preserving uncertainty and tracing how historical knowledge is produced.</p><p>DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.22816706 · CC BY-NC-ND 4.0</p><p><a class="text-link" href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22816706">Read and download from Zenodo</a></p></section><section id="foundation" class="prose-section"><h2>Related foundational work</h2><h3><em>Los tejedores de memorias</em></h3><p>Edgardo Civallero · 2023 · Thesis · Spanish</p><p>The thesis develops the epistemic framework underlying Galapagensis: documentary work as the recovery, connection, interpretation and activation of heterogeneous fragments of memory and knowledge. It predates the independent programme.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19054301">Read the thesis on Zenodo</a></p></section><section id="offline" class="prose-section"><h2>Galapagensis to go</h2><p>The offline-access programme is intended for readers, schools and communities with limited or unreliable connectivity. Future resources may include PDFs, EPUBs, print-friendly teaching materials and thematic packages derived from the same research corpus. No offline packages are offered on this page yet.</p></section><section id="reuse" class="prose-section"><h2>Citation and reuse</h2><p>When citing a publication, include its author or editor, title, publication date and publisher, together with its DOI or stable URL. Identify the edition or version where relevant, particularly when a work has been revised.</p><p>Each publication carries its own rights and licence conditions. Consult those notices before reproducing, adapting, translating or redistributing material, and retain the credits attached to any third-party content.</p><p><a href="/rights-and-use/">Rights, Licensing &amp; Use</a></p></section></article></div></section>
